node.doctext:
I'm using TinyPerl 5.8. Why am I getting an error in this script??? I am fiddling around with functions to see what happens when I modify my code. And according to the manual, this should work. And yet it doesn't work! Why?

<P>Btw, I am trying to learn how to use "virtual functions" in Perl. Is there a better way than doing it like this?: my $Func = sub { ... };

<code>
use strict;
use warnings;

my $myFunction = sub { print "Hey, I am from Italy! @_\n"; };

printList(1, 2, 3, 4);

$myFunction = sub { print "Hey, I am from Japan! @_\n"; };

printList(5, 6, 7);


sub printList
{
  print "\nprintList was called.\n";
  &$myFunction->();
}
exit;

#
# This program should print:
#
# printList was called.
# Hey, I am from Italy! 1 2 3 4
# printList was called.
# Hey, I am from Japan! 5 6 7
#

</code>
